       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. The risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity. A single 2,400 mg dose already exceeds what's recommended for one administration, which is usually 800 mg.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day). I can enter either one now.\n- **Add a note** to any order, for example \"Pain control, discussed with attending.\"\n- **Help you reach a different goal.** If the aim is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for this dose, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. Once they've approved a specific regimen, I can enter that order."
